{
  "an9.6:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 9.6 ",
  "an9.6:0.2": "1. Awakening ",
  "an9.6:0.3": "Association ",
  "an9.6:1.1": "There Sāriputta addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an9.6:2.1": "“Reverends, you should distinguish two two kinds of individual: ",
  "an9.6:2.2": "those you should associate with, and those you shouldn’t associate with. ",
  "an9.6:2.3": "You should distinguish two kinds of robes: ",
  "an9.6:2.4": "those you should wear, and those you shouldn’t wear. ",
  "an9.6:2.5": "You should distinguish two kinds of almsfood: ",
  "an9.6:2.6": "that which you should eat, and that which you shouldn’t eat. ",
  "an9.6:2.7": "You should distinguish two kinds of lodging: ",
  "an9.6:2.8": "those you should frequent, and those you shouldn’t frequent. ",
  "an9.6:2.9": "You should distinguish two kinds of village or town: ",
  "an9.6:2.10": "those you should frequent, and those you shouldn’t frequent. ",
  "an9.6:2.11": "You should distinguish two kinds of country: ",
  "an9.6:2.12": "those you should frequent, and those you shouldn’t frequent. ",
  "an9.6:3.1": "‘You should distinguish two two kinds of individual: ",
  "an9.6:3.2": "those you should associate with, and those you shouldn’t associate with.’ ",
  "an9.6:3.3": "That’s what I said, but why did I say it? ",
  "an9.6:3.4": "Well, should you know of an individual: ",
  "an9.6:3.5": "‘When I associate with this individual, unskillful qualities grow, and skillful qualities decline. ",
  "an9.6:3.6": "And the necessities of lif